  "notes": "Drawn from N856SY (Aug 2024), checked on N843SY (Feb 2026). The navy's contour lines and the fin's rays are reduced to their color fields. A few aircraft still wear the earlier blue scheme (blue with light rays forward, an orange line, white below) with the new lower-case titles: N805SY in October 2026. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N856SY fitted to the measured 737-800 shape (its windows land on the shape's): the fuselage areas match the photo; the title runs x 0.149 to 0.416, its baseline a little below the windows (y -0.05, it had been drawn on the window line), the t's top at y 0.55, lowercase 0.91 of it (Sun Country's lettering has very short ascenders).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2018 livery replaced the blue scheme, which survives on a few aircraft."
